# EF Core (`apps/platform`)

## DbContext

`EnterpriseDbContext` owns Identity and security audit data. Compile-time modules may contribute model configuration through `IEntityModelContributor`.

## Entity configuration

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — inherit BaseEntityConfiguration<T>
public sealed class ExampleModelContributor : IEntityModelContributor
{
    public void Configure(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)
    {
        var builder = modelBuilder.Entity<Example>();
        builder.Property(e => e.Name).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(200);
        builder.ToTable("Examples");
    }
}
```

## Migrations

- Folder: `apps/platform/Migrations/`
- Create with `--project apps/platform --startup-project apps/api`
- Dev/Aspire: `InitializeEnterpriseDatabaseAsync` runs `MigrateAsync()` when configured
- Compose: one-shot `migrator` service
- **Never** `EnsureCreated()`

## Seeding

The initializer synchronizes protected role permissions and optionally creates the bootstrap admin with a required password change.

## Provider

PostgreSQL-only. Connection comes from `ConnectionStrings:enterprisestarterdb` (Aspire) or `Database:ConnectionString`.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
Database.EnsureCreated();
options.UseSqlite(...);

// ✅ GOOD
await context.Database.MigrateAsync();
options.UseNpgsql(connectionString);
```
